    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0962" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg812"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Wilson to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-11-13"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 13, 1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 249.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that in
                    accordance with the constitutional provision the Belgian Parliament convened on
                    the second Tuesday of November.</p>
                <pb facs="0963" n="813" xml:id="pg813"/>
                <p>The deliberation of the Parliament during the present session will be directed to
                    a solution of the question of the annexation of the Kongo to Belgium, and this
                    important measure will take precedence of all others.</p>
                <p>The proceedings of Parliament will be observed with interest and reported to the
                    department from time to time.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane
                    Wilson</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
